messages.text:
We can accept the addendum in principle, with the following to settle custody, qualification and signoff.

We do not currently hold the affected revision in full. However, our specialist machining shop has already cut stock for the original fixture using an earlier controlled extract. It does not hold page 4 or the full drawing. We will immediately quarantine that cut stock and the related extract, suspend further use and onward transfer, and include both in the destruction certificate unless you direct otherwise. Please advise whether that existing stock is to be destroyed now or held in quarantine; it will not be used for the affected step without your written approval.

On coupon qualification, the low-level vibration sweep can qualify the reference coupon only if the test plan includes a geometry-free acceptance envelope and explicit tolerances. We propose the following measured quantities unless your test requirements state otherwise:

- response quantity: drive-point and one response accelerometer transfer function magnitude and phase;
- frequency range: the full planned test range, to be stated in the test plan;
- tolerance: ±1 dB magnitude and ±10 degrees phase, with coherence above 0.95 at evaluation frequencies.

If you supply a different envelope, we can work to that. Without an agreed envelope and tolerances, the coupon cannot qualify.

On repeatability and signoff, our test lead will measure the reference coupon at the testing house and send the machining shop a tolerance table only if the design owner specifies feature tolerances and agrees in writing that the repeatability check is the qualifying method. We propose that the verification result be submitted to you for written acceptance before the coupon is used in the affected test step. If the coupon fails verification, the affected step remains on hold until we agree on a correction.

Custody will be as follows:

- the reference coupon is logged with a unique ID;
- it remains the design owner’s property;
- it is stored in the testing house’s secure area;
- it is not transferred to the machining shop or any other external recipient;
- it is returned or destroyed at the design owner’s direction after final report acceptance.

The two-day preparation period should start only after we have agreed in writing on the verification method, response quantities, frequency range and tolerance. Verification and your written acceptance may add time separately. Work independent of the restricted geometry will proceed in the meantime.
